 "deploy_attempt_1": {
  "started": "2026-11-15T22:46:57.257Z",
  "outcome": "FAILED at the ECR digest check, before anything reached the instance",
  "what_was_wrong": "deploy.sh copied GHCR to ECR with `docker buildx imagetools create --tag <ecr>:<sha> <ghcr>@<digest>`. publish.yml's image is a single-platform manifest (v2 schema 2), and given one, imagetools does not copy it as is: it pushed a new one-entry manifest list, sha256:729dc0bc..., under the tag. deploy.sh's post-copy check (ECR digest must equal the published digest) stopped the run. The local test before merge copied hello-world, which is already a manifest list, so it kept its digest and missed this.",
  "fix": "scripts/deploy.sh now pulls the published digest from GHCR, tags it and pushes it to ECR (docker pull / tag / push), keeping the same check. With Docker Desktop's containerd image store the pushed manifest is byte-identical. The wrong ECR image (tag 07f6f63..., digest 729dc0bc...) was removed with `aws ecr batch-delete-image` (ECR tags are immutable), the only AWS change outside deploy.sh, terraform and the one-shots. deploy.sh's message for that case now prints that command.",
  "ecr_delete": {
   "imageIds": [
    {
     "imageDigest": "sha256:729dc0bc11d57106a0d9e7bfe2ecfb042508ad15e056ad56ddf8688f211d2c4a",
     "imageTag": "07f6f638a7570394cb6023ce1d5fa8f67418a3b1"
    }
   ],
